From: Banks Troutman <banks.troutman@oxos.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: cs42xx8: Tegra compatibility fixes

Three fixes for CS42448 on NVIDIA Tegra:

1. set_dai_sysclk: ignore freq < 1MHz. The Tegra machine driver's
   SFC init callback passes the sample rate (e.g. 48000) as the
   sysclk frequency, clobbering the real MCLK rate cached from
   clk_get_rate() at probe. Guard against this.

2. hw_params ratio: use DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST instead of integer
   truncation. Tegra's PLLA produces 12287996 Hz instead of exact
   12288000. At 48kHz, truncation gives ratio=255 (rejected);
   rounding gives 256 (valid).

3. probe: add msleep(5) between reset assert and de-assert.
   CS42448 datasheet section 4.9 requires minimum 1ms RST# low
   pulse width.

Signed-off-by: Banks Troutman <banks.troutman@oxos.com>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/cs42xx8.c | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/cs42xx8.c b/sound/soc/codecs/cs42xx8.c
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/cs42xx8.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/cs42xx8.c
@@ -206,7 +206,9 @@ static int cs42xx8_set_dai_sysclk(struct snd_soc_dai *codec_dai,
 	struct snd_soc_component *component = codec_dai->component;
 	struct cs42xx8_priv *cs42xx8 = snd_soc_component_get_drvdata(component);

-	cs42xx8->sysclk = freq;
+	/* Ignore sample-rate values passed by machine drivers (e.g. Tegra) */
+	if (freq >= 1000000)
+		cs42xx8->sysclk = freq;

 	return 0;
 }
@@ -278,8 +280,8 @@ static int cs42xx8_hw_params(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream,
 	rate[tx]  = params_rate(params);
 	rate[!tx] = cs42xx8->rate[!tx];

-	ratio[tx] = rate[tx] > 0 ? cs42xx8->sysclk / rate[tx] : 0;
-	ratio[!tx] = rate[!tx] > 0 ? cs42xx8->sysclk / rate[!tx] : 0;
+	ratio[tx] = rate[tx] > 0 ? DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST(cs42xx8->sysclk, rate[tx]) : 0;
+	ratio[!tx] = rate[!tx] > 0 ? DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST(cs42xx8->sysclk, rate[!tx]) : 0;

 	/* Get functional mode for tx and rx according to rate */
 	for (i = 0; i < 2; i++) {
@@ -554,6 +556,9 @@ int cs42xx8_probe(struct device *dev, struct regmap *regmap)
 	if (IS_ERR(cs42xx8->gpiod_reset))
 		return PTR_ERR(cs42xx8->gpiod_reset);

+	/* CS42448 requires minimum 1ms RST# low pulse (datasheet section 4.9) */
+	msleep(5);
+
 	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(cs42xx8->gpiod_reset, 0);

 	cs42xx8->clk = devm_clk_get(dev, "mclk");
